---
description: Never print API keys, tokens, or secret values in chat
alwaysApply: true
---

# No secrets in chat

- Never print, quote, or paraphrase secret values in assistant messages (API keys, bearer tokens, passwords, private keys, webhook secrets, env values, abracadabra vault contents).
- If a tool or shell returns secrets, refer to them by name only (e.g. `OPENAI_API_KEY`) and say they were retrieved or set — do not paste values.
- Prefer writing secrets to env files, keychain, or abracadabra; never echo them into the conversation.
- If the user insists on proof of a value, mask it: short prefix + `…` only (e.g. `abra_a1b2…`).
- Do not put secrets in commits, logs, PR bodies, issue comments, or code comments.
